                "text": "This avoidable government shutdown is impacting 1.3 million active-duty service members, delaying checks for 1.9 million civilian employees, and leaving over 100,000 federal law-enforcement officers working without pay. It halts small-business loans and risks nutrition assistance for women and children.\n\nThe economic toll is severe: each week a shutdown drags on, it costs the nation about $15 billion in GDP and could put 43,000 Americans out of work if it lasts a month.\n\nAll while the latest proposal prioritizes funding new healthcare coverage for illegal immigrants.\n\nWe need to reopen the government and get back to legislating responsibly.",
